{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119233538f1d255f6215b4c74","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Pins test green (24 assertions). Now the cross-host corpus reference (B3 part 2). Plan:\n\n1. Define the canonical reference cases: for each map-corpus label + each set-corpus label + each size (8/9/16/32 for both maps and sets), build ONE canonical form and digest-snapshot it.\n2. Capture the snapshots on the JVM via a scratch namespace (reusing the REAL namespace's helpers? They're private... The scratch can require the test namespace? Private vars aren't accessible. Simplest: the capture namespace replicates build+snapshot by requiring yang.clojure-collection-order-test and using its PUBLIC vars — everything relevant is private. Alternative: make the capture a deftest INSIDE the namespace that PRINTS the snapshots, run it, paste, then convert to assertions. I'll add a temporary deftest in the real namespace that prints the reference bundle, run, capture output, replace the printing deftest with the recorded-literal assertion deftest.\n\nThe case list (19 cases): map-corpus labels (7): constant-keys-dynamic-values, dynamic-keys, heterogeneous-keys, nested-collections, floats, duplicate-subtrees — wait count: [:constant-keys-dynamic-values :dynamic-keys :heterogeneous-keys :nested-collections :floats :duplicate-subtrees] = 6 (same-key-different-values was removed in r1). Set corpus (4): dynamic-elements, nested-dynamic-sets, colliding-value-expressions, heterogeneous-elements. Sizes: 8/9/16/32 × {map, set} = 8. Total 18 cases.\n\nSnapshot function: digest-snapshot (project-batch (yang/compile form)) — with case id.\n\nWrite the temporary printing deftest now.","signature":"b6c4a58b5f804367b20578bb"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"854a