{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20261119234852b47d2569c82746c4","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The transfer test PASSED (all 12 of its assertions — no failures listed for it). The set-trace test: derived expected `[2 :s1 0 0]` vs actual `[:s1 0 0]` — the actual log has only THREE entries and no `2` — the literal `2` element has no tap, so it logs nothing! My `expected` includes 2 for the literal element — but the literal never taps. Fix: expected should include an entry only for TAPPED elements — the literal 2's \"arg-value\" shouldn't appear in the log. But its POSITION in the canonical order still matters for the others' relative order... The log only records taps. Expected = (filter some / map with nil for untapped then remove nil): keep the canonical ORDER derivation over all elements, project to tap args, DROP the untapped one:\n\n```clojure\nexpected (into [] (comp (map arg-value) (remove nil?)) ordered)\n```\nwith arg-value returning nil for the literal 2 (no tap). Set arg-value map without the `2 2` entry → lookup nil → removed. Count assertion: `(= 3 (count expected))` with 2 zeros + :s1.","signature":"89878abbbf354a2b9e925b78"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"03bcb0fb-1426-4d54-b363-a6e83e99f131","timestamp":"2026-11-19T15:49:02.091Z","thinking_duration_ms":4301,"thinking_display":"updates"}
