{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_d696715f844d431b846c0b45","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: fixorder-r1-round-status\n3\tdescription: constructed-collection-order r1+r2 done 2026-11-19 (review F1-F3 resolved, JVM/Node/Dart green, Jolt blocked by inherited J2 refusal; uncommitted)\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-18T20:38:00.319Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tfix/constructed-collection-order r1 (ruling 1795017757000) + r2 (review 1795030110000 F1-F3) implemented 2026-11-19 in datomworld-fixorder @ 706d44f9, NOTHING committed. Emitter `compile-constructed-collection` sorts map pairs by `jing/canonical-compare` over `[key-root value-root]` (set elements by root, vectors untouched) via new `content-root` helper; manifest c1-2 + `:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1`. Ruled arity-map order: fn, reason, argc (key roots 1e0366/81b62c/8930bf). Only cohort members argument-vector + lower-unit changed bytes; pre-fix bundle archived as cc4-replay-snapshots-prefix-c1-1.edn (sha 5f28913f… matches r2 reviewer pin). Gates r2: JVM 46/605 + 10/91392 + combined 56/91997; Node 10/91392; Dart ordering ALL 10 PASSED; Jolt exit-1 at manifest (4 inherited unlisted namespaces — owner dependency, recorded); kondo 0 errors/1 pre-existing warning.\n12\t\n13\tNaN tie traps (r2, reviewer-sustained): the set-element tie IS constructable — `(conj (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]) <dynamic>)` keeps both NaNs stably; but a SINGLE `into` session mixing a SEQ element with the NaN pair LOSES one NaN on the JVM (hash collision ruled out), `hash-set`/persistent `conj` chains collapse under Java equals, `(into {} ...)` map collapses while `assoc` keeps — retention is per-constructor, never map-vs-set. r1's \"unconstructable\" claim was a misdiagnosis: count assertions calibrated to a collapsed set failed on actual RETENTION+reorder. NaN literals: map/set literals reject dup NaN keys at read; build at runtime.\n14\t\n15\tOther traps: ClojureDart has NO `array-map` (reader-conditional insertion-map); host `=` ignores metadata so metadata-variant keys collapse silently; standalone `yang/compile` defaults tail?=true so independent builders use `(compile-form x false {})`; debruijn machines take `:free-env`; shadow `--config-merge` needs literal `\\\\.` in the arg (4 backslashes in the driver file); children need JAVA_HOME=mise java/21. Permission gate: only `clojure -M:test` direct; the rest via temp test namespace + ProcessBuilder (deleted at delivery); heredoc python writes trip a brace-with-quote filter.\n16\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345","uuid":"f71203c8-4635-4951-936c-d539f314fc0b","timestamp":"2026-11-19T16:35:09.120Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/.claude-glm/projects/-Users-sto-workspace-datomworld/memory/fixorder-r1-round-status.md","content":"---\nname: fixorder-r1-round-status\ndescription: constructed-collection-order r1+r2 done 2026-11-19 (review F1-F3 resolved, JVM/Node/Dart green, Jolt blocked by inherited J2 refusal; uncommitted)\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 3b22ab98-3808-492f-99b7-216dd4cf8345\n  modified: 2026-11-18T20:38:00.319Z\n---\n\nfix/constructed-collection-order r1 (ruling 1795017757000) + r2 (review 1795030110000 F1-F3) implemented 2026-11-19 in datomworld-fixorder @ 706d44f9, NOTHING committed. Emitter `compile-constructed-collection` sorts map pairs by `jing/canonical-compare` over `[key-root value-root]` (set elements by root, vectors untouched) via new `content-root` helper; manifest c1-2 + `:yang.clojure/constructed-collections-v1`. Ruled arity-map order: fn, reason, argc (key roots 1e0366/81b62c/8930bf). Only cohort members argument-vector + lower-unit changed bytes; pre-fix bundle archived as cc4-replay-snapshots-prefix-c1-1.edn (sha 5f28913f… matches r2 reviewer pi